🔢 1️⃣ Bubble Sort
🔹 Idea (Meaning)

Compare adjacent elements

Swap if they are in the wrong order

Largest element “bubbles up” to the end

🔹 Example

Array:

5  1  4  2


Pass 1

(5,1) → swap → 1 5 4 2

(5,4) → swap → 1 4 5 2

(5,2) → swap → 1 4 2 5

Largest element 5 is at correct position.

🔹 Code Explanation
for(int i = 0; i < n-1; i++)


Number of passes

for(int j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++)


Compare adjacent elements

if(arr[j] > arr[j+1])
    swap(arr[j], arr[j+1]);


Swap if order is wrong

🔹 Time Complexity

Best: O(n)

Worst: O(n²)

🔢 2️⃣ Selection Sort
🔹 Idea

Find the smallest element

Place it at the correct position

🔹 Example

Array:

3  1  4  2


Find smallest → 1

Swap with first element

Result:

1  3  4  2

🔹 Code Explanation
int min = i;


Assume current index is minimum

if(arr[j] < arr[min])
    min = j;


Find smallest element

swap(arr[i], arr[min]);


Place smallest element correctly

🔹 Time Complexity

Best/Worst: O(n²)

🔢 3️⃣ Insertion Sort
🔹 Idea

Insert each element into its correct position

Like sorting playing cards

🔹 Example

Array:

4  3  5  1


Insert 3 before 4

3  4  5  1

🔹 Code Explanation
int key = arr[i];


Element to insert

while(j >= 0 && arr[j] > key)


Shift elements to right

arr[j+1] = key;


Insert key at correct position

🔹 Time Complexity

Best: O(n)

Worst: O(n²)

🔢 4️⃣ Merge Sort
🔹 Idea

Divide array into halves

Sort halves

Merge them

🔹 Example
8  3  2  9
→ {8,3} {2,9}
→ {3,8} {2,9}
→ {2,3,8,9}

🔹 Why Merge Sort is fast

Always divides array

Uses Divide and Conquer

🔹 Time Complexity

Best/Worst: O(n log n)

🔢 5️⃣ Quick Sort
🔹 Idea

Choose a pivot

Place pivot in correct position

Sort left & right parts

🔹 Example
10  7  8  9  1
Pivot = 1
→ { } 1 {10 7 8 9}

🔹 Pivot Meaning

Pivot = element used to divide array

🔹 Time Complexity

Best: O(n log n)

Worst: O(n²)

🔢 6️⃣ Heap Sort
🔹 Idea

Convert array into Max Heap

Remove largest element repeatedly

🔹 Example
4  10  3  5
→ Max Heap → 10 5 3 4
→ Sorted → 3 4 5 10

🔹 Time Complexity

Best/Worst: O(n log n)

